WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.010
Cloud GPUs are strongest when demand is temporary, uncertain,

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:05.740
or larger than local capacity.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.740
A team can rent a high-memory accelerator for a short evaluation,

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:10.400
absorb a temporary batch backlog,

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.487
or test whether a model benefits from hardware that would be expensive to purchase.

00:00:14.487 --> 00:00:18.535
Burst capacity also helps when a normal local environment is sufficient most of the time

00:00:18.535 --> 00:00:20.840
but a deadline creates a short-lived peak.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.612
Shared remote access can make cloud resources attractive to distributed teams.

00:00:24.612 --> 00:00:27.470
A controlled environment can provide consistent drivers, tools,

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:30.520
and data paths without shipping hardware to every participant.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.595
Cloud deployment also places inference closer to applications already running in the same

00:00:34.595 --> 00:00:34.875
provider,

00:00:34.875 --> 00:00:36.680
which may reduce integration effort.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.960
These benefits depend on identity controls, regional availability, network behavior,

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.920
and a reproducible setup rather than on the GPU alone.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.530
Local hardware may be cheaper for steady, high utilization over a long period,

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.755
especially when power and maintenance are manageable.

00:00:49.755 --> 00:00:53.100
It can offer lower latency for local data, simpler privacy boundaries,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.560
and guaranteed access to a known device.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.880
Cloud capacity may be unavailable in a preferred region, constrained by account quota,

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.560
or expensive once storage and transfer are included.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:06.545
Moving a large private dataset into and out of the cloud can erase the convenience of fast

00:01:06.545 --> 00:01:07.395
provisioning.

00:01:07.395 --> 00:01:08.965
Compare the complete workload.

00:01:08.965 --> 00:01:13.430
Estimate active hours, utilization, storage duration, transfer volume, engineering time,

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:15.040
and the cost of interruptions.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.600
Consider whether the data is permitted in the chosen environment.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.560
A useful decision is rarely cloud versus local forever.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.860
Many organizations use local compute for predictable daily work and rent cloud GPUs for

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.070
experiments,

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.320
temporary scale, or specialized memory requirements.
